[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3587377137","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113231#issuecomment-3587377137","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113231","id":3587377137,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7V0wfx","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-27T22:01:20Z","updated_at":"2025-11-27T22:01:20Z","body":"> using a 3D scene with a WorldBoundary3D at the bottom, spawning 300-400 RigidBody3D's (Half of them Capsules, Half Cubes) high above the ground, letting them fall, which exits after 4 seconds, and the results are:\r\n\r\nCan you upload the test project here? I'd like to run benchmarks locally.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3587377137/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3588441839","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113231#issuecomment-3588441839","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113231","id":3588441839,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7V40bv","user":{"login":"SourceOfHTML","id":70210240,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwMjEwMjQw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70210240?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SourceOfHTML","html_url":"https://github.com/SourceOfHTML","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SourceOfHTML/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SourceOfHTML/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SourceOfHTML/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SourceOfHTML/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SourceOfHTML/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SourceOfHTML/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SourceOfHTML/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SourceOfHTML/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SourceOfHTML/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-28T09:00:23Z","updated_at":"2025-11-28T09:00:23Z","body":"I've updated the post with the test project and rebased the branch","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3588441839/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4978706311","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113231#issuecomment-4978706311","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113231","id":4978706311,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABKMEHhw","user":{"login":"rburing","id":229837,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTgzNw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/229837?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing","html_url":"https://github.com/rburing","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rburing/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-15T08:50:31Z","updated_at":"2026-07-15T08:50:31Z","body":"Can you explain the algorithm and why it's correct? Ideally with a reference to the literature or another physics engine.\r\n\r\nWhen the capsule and box are aligned and touching along an edge, you should get *two* contact points, which doesn't seem to be handled in the code.\r\n\r\nAlso note you are touching GodotPhysics3D code, while the new default and recommended physics engine is Jolt Physics. I would only recommend spending further time on this if you're using Godot Physics yourself and it's affecting your own project.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4978706311/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4981370306","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113231#issuecomment-4981370306","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113231","id":4981370306,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABKOmtwg","user":{"login":"SourceOfHTML","id":70210240,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwMjEwMjQw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/70210240?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SourceOfHTML","html_url":"https://github.com/SourceOfHTML","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SourceOfHTML/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SourceOfHTML/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SourceOfHTML/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SourceOfHTML/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SourceOfHTML/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SourceOfHTML/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SourceOfHTML/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SourceOfHTML/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SourceOfHTML/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-15T13:53:33Z","updated_at":"2026-07-15T13:53:33Z","body":"I'm spending time on this partially out of my own self-interest. I've realized how useless it is to work on a physics engine that's being phased out, but it's still fun and enlightening. Still, noted and thanks.\r\n\r\nI didn't use any external literature, or any insights gleamed from other physics engines to write this code. I only looked at code that already existed within the same file.\r\n\r\nIn `_collision_sphere_box`, you'll find an algorithm that as far as I remember when I looked into it, is using black magic (read: Transform3D projections) to find the nearest point on the box to the sphere, and using basic maths beyond that point to figure out if and where a collision is happening.\r\n\r\nIn `_collision_sphere_capsule`, you'll find that the entire code in this function is for finding the closest point on the capsule to the sphere. That info is passed to `analytic_sphere_collision`, which handles the sphere collisions that we're all familiar with.\r\n\r\nWhat I did (aside from being very confused as to what a `_CollectorCallback` is), was take the \"Turn a capsule into a sphere\" from the second part, the \"Find the closest point on a box to the sphere center\" from the first part, and mash them together in a forbidden marriage that neither side approved of.\r\n\r\n(Side note: At first, I'd put the collision points the other way around on accident, and the boxes and capsules, instead of colliding, made vigorous love to each other. It floored me.)\r\n\r\nI'm mostly being facetious, but that is the extent of what I did. The only part of the code that I shamelessly copy-pasted with little-to-no changes was the `_collision_sphere_box` one, because every time I try to figure out what exactly `Transform3D.xform()` does, I die inside a little and doubt myself as a maths nerd (seriously, it confuses me every time, even though I'm fairly comfortable with vector maths conceptually).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4981370306/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]